    {
      "chunk_id": "a4993680c845d5ca3bdcb3cd2e553b97b602a6c99e7854fb37518d9ed1755f99_chunk_0002",
      "document_id": "a4993680c845d5ca3bdcb3cd2e553b97b602a6c99e7854fb37518d9ed1755f99",
      "chunk_index": 2,
      "text": "Abstract:\n\nStudents at SR University routinely struggle to find accurate, up-to-date information scattered across syllabi, academic calendars, exam schedules, and departmental notices, often relying on outdated PDFs or word-of-mouth. SRU Assistant addresses this by combining a RAG pipeline with the university's own academic documents to deliver accurate, source-grounded answers to natural language queries. The system ingests institutional documents such as course structures, semester calendars, and exam guidelines, converts them into vector embeddings, and stores them in a searchable vector database. When a student poses a query, the system retrieves the most relevant document segments and passes them to a large language model to generate a precise, context-aware response with citations to the source material. This eliminates hallucinated or generic answers common in standalone chatbots and ensures every response is traceable to an official university document. The framework is designed to be extensible to additional departments and document types, providing a scalable foundation for intelligent academic support systems.\n\nAPPROVAL",
